-- Broadcasting Act (Cap 28): the First Schedule with THREE items.
--
-- Sources: the Revised Edition 2012 (31 August 2012), quoted by plain `src:N`, and the Revised Edition 2003
-- (31 July 2003), quoted as `src:BA1994.20030731:N`.  The two editions print the same Schedule: the same three
-- items and the same three definitions; the 2003 edition's quotation marks are doubled single quotes, which the
-- gate treats as punctuation.  Raw files: subjects/sg/broadcasting-act-1994/registers/source-bundle/
-- BA1994.20120831.txt and BA1994.20030731.txt.
--
-- This module has NO time built-ins: it says what the three-item text says and nothing about when it governs.
-- When it governs is decided in sgbau-first-schedule.l4.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgbau-nouns`

§ `First Schedule, three items`

-- src:2167 | 1. Broadcast television receiver.
-- src:2173 | “broadcast television receiver” means any apparatus used for the visual and
-- src:2174 | aural reception in monochrome or colour of any broadcasting service;
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2139 | 1. Broadcast television receiver.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2148 | ‘‘broadcast television receiver’’ means any apparatus used for the visual and
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2149 | aural reception in monochrome or colour of any broadcasting service;
@ref Broadcasting Act (Cap 28), First Schedule, item 1 and its definition (src:2167-2174; src:BA1994.20030731:2139-2149)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`item 1 of the three-item Schedule, a broadcast television receiver` MEANS
    apparatus's `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service`

-- src:2168 | 2. Broadcast sound receiver.
-- src:2171 | “broadcast sound receiver” means any apparatus used for the aural reception
-- src:2172 | of any broadcasting service;
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2141 | 2. Broadcast sound receiver.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2146 | ‘‘broadcast sound receiver’’ means any apparatus used for the aural
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2147 | reception of any broadcasting service;
@ref Broadcasting Act (Cap 28), First Schedule, item 2 and its definition (src:2168-2172; src:BA1994.20030731:2141-2147)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`item 2 of the three-item Schedule, a broadcast sound receiver` MEANS
    apparatus's `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service`

-- src:2169 | 3. Television receive-only satellite receiving system (TVRO system).
-- src:2175 | “television receive-only satellite receiving system” means any apparatus
-- src:2176 | (including a dish antenna) or any combination of apparatus capable of
-- src:2177 | direct reception of any broadcasting service emitted from or passing
-- src:2178 | through any communication or broadcast satellite in extra-terrestrial space.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2143 | 3. Television receive-only satellite receiving system (TVRO system).
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2150 | ‘‘television receive-only satellite receiving system’’ means any apparatus
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2151 | (including a dish antenna) or any combination of apparatus capable of
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2152 | direct reception of any broadcasting service emitted from or passing
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2153 | through any communication or broadcast satellite in extra-terrestrial
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2154 | space.
@ref Broadcasting Act (Cap 28), First Schedule, item 3 and its definition (src:2169-2178; src:BA1994.20030731:2143-2154)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`item 3 of the three-item Schedule, a TVRO system` MEANS
    apparatus's `capable of direct reception from a satellite in extra-terrestrial space`

-- "BROADCASTING APPARATUS" heads the Schedule, and s 2(1) says "specified in the First Schedule": the Schedule
-- specifies an apparatus when any item fits it.
-- src:2163 | FIRST SCHEDULE
-- src:2164 | Section 2(1)
-- src:2166 | BROADCASTING APPARATUS
-- src:2170 | For the purposes of this Schedule —
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2134 | FIRST SCHEDULE
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2135 | Section 2 (1)
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2137 | BROADCASTING APPARATUS
-- src:BA1994.20030731:2145 | For the purposes of this Schedule —
@ref Broadcasting Act (Cap 28), First Schedule, heading and the words introducing the definitions (src:2163-2170; src:BA1994.20030731:2134-2145)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the three-item Schedule specifies the apparatus` MEANS
        `item 1 of the three-item Schedule, a broadcast television receiver` apparatus
    OR  `item 2 of the three-item Schedule, a broadcast sound receiver` apparatus
    OR  `item 3 of the three-item Schedule, a TVRO system` apparatus
